# Public https URL identifying the Tumult application to the identity provider.
#
# This is NOT the dev server's address. MAS rejects http, and rejects localhost
# under any scheme, so it cannot be derived from window.location during local
# development. Any https URL you control works — it is shown to the user on the
# consent screen and is not fetched during login.
#
# The redirect URI is derived from the origin the app is actually served from,
# so a localhost dev server still receives the callback.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and set the value. Both files live
# at the REPO ROOT, not in apps/web: `apps/web/vite.config.ts` sets `envDir` to
# the root so the local build and the Vercel build (`vercel pull` writes
# `.vercel/.env.production.local` into its working directory, the repo root)
# read env from the same place. Putting it in apps/web instead means the build
# silently proceeds without it and the app throws during import — a blank page.
VITE_CLIENT_URI=https://example.com
